.TH QTOP 1 "2026-11-10" "qtop 0.9.20261110" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
qtop \- text-mode monitor of batch-cluster utilization and job status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qtop
.RB [ \-FGT ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B qtop \-w
.RI [ seconds ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B qtop \-R
.I datetime
.RI [ duration ]
.br
.B qtop \-\-load\-sample
.I archive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qtop
queries a batch scheduler (PBS/Torque, SGE, Slurm or OAR) and prints three
sections on one screen:
.TP
.B Job Accounting Summary
running and queued jobs per queue or partition, and node and core totals.
.TP
.B Worker Node Occupancy
a matrix with one column per worker node and one row per core; each cell
shows the user (by an id letter and color) whose job occupies that core.
.TP
.B User Accounts and Pool Mappings
the per-user legend for the matrix, with job counts by state.
.PP
Without
.BR \-w ,
qtop prints once and exits. Scheduler output is saved under
.I savepath
(see
.BR FILES ),
so a view can be replayed later with
.BR \-R .
The
.B demo
scheduler generates a synthetic cluster and needs no scheduler commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Scheduler and input
.TP
.BI \-b " name" "\fR, \fP" \-\-batchSystem " name"
Scheduler to query:
.BR pbs ,
.BR sge ,
.BR slurm ,
.BR oar ,
.B demo
or
.B auto
(detect from the commands found in
.BR PATH ).
.TP
.BI \-s " path" "\fR, \fP" \-\-SetSourceDir " path"
Read scheduler traces from a directory or a tar archive instead of running
scheduler commands; a plain output file selects its parent directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-load\-sample " archive"
Reproduce an anonymized support snapshot (made with
.BR "\-L \-A" )
without scheduler commands.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Include hidden and group-unavailable partitions in live Slurm queries
(subject to permissions).
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-get_GECOS_via_getent_passwd
Look up user details with
.B getent passwd
for every user in the scheduler output.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-StrictCheck
Compare the running-job total reported by the scheduler with the jobs qtop
found and displayed.
.SS Display
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-disablesection1
Hide the Job Accounting Summary.
.TP
.BR \-2 ", " \-\-disablesection2
Hide the Worker Node Occupancy matrix.
.TP
.BR \-3 ", " \-\-disablesection3
Hide the User Accounts and Pool Mappings.
.TP
.BR \-4 ", " \-\-accounttotals
Add a totals row to the User Accounts and Pool Mappings.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-COLOR " " \fBON\fP | \fBOFF\fP | \fBAUTO\fP
Color output.
.B AUTO
(the default) uses color on a terminal; see
.B QTOP_COLOR
in
.BR ENVIRONMENT .
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-classic
Mimic the legacy qtop display as far as possible.
.TP
.BR \-\-expand\-queues
Show one queue or partition per line in the accounting summary (toggle with
.B Q
in watch mode).
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-groups
Show each active user's primary Unix group in the account table.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-ForceNames
Show node names instead of numbered worker nodes, even for small clusters.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-blindremapping
Number worker nodes in order of appearance; for node names that are not a
plain arithmetic sequence (for example Rocks clusters).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-noMasking
Do not hide leading empty worker nodes (by default, if the first 30 nodes
are unused, numbering starts at 31).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-removeemptycorelines
Remove matrix rows consisting only of non-existent cores
.RB ( # ).
Given twice
.RB ( \-rr ),
also remove rows of free cores
.RB ( _ ).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-Transpose
Rotate the matrix by 90 degrees.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-less
Let the matrix overflow the terminal width, for piping into
.BR "less \-RS" .
.SS Run modes
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch " [\fIseconds\fP]"
Refresh like
.BR watch (1)
every
.I seconds
(default 2), with interactive navigation (see
.BR "INTERACTIVE COMMANDS" ).
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-replay " \fIdatetime\fP [\fIduration\fP]"
Replay saved output from
.IR datetime ,
given as
.I yyyymmddTHHMMSS
(e.g. 20161118T182300),
.I HHMM
(today) or
.I mmddTHHMM
(this year).
.I duration
is
.IR N h,
.IR N m
or
.IR N s
(default 2m).
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-onlysavetofile
Save results without printing them.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-export
Export cluster data as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-sample
Create a support archive with the log, the scheduler output and the qtop
output. With
.BR \-A ,
store a portable masked snapshot instead. Given twice
.RB ( \-LL ),
also add package sources and runtime assets and, without
.BR \-A ,
the bundled defaults and effective configuration.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-anonymize
Mask identifiers where the backend supports it (requires
.BR \-e ).
.TP
.B \-\-raw\-companion
With
.BR "\-L \-A \-e" ,
also save a separate, private archive of the unmasked scheduler input.
.TP
.B \-\-masked\-traces
With
.BR "\-L \-A \-e" ,
add experimental masked scheduler-format traces; unsupported files are
omitted.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.BI \-f " file" "\fR, \fP" \-\-setCUSTOMCONFFILE " file"
Use
.I file
as the custom configuration (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.TP
.BI \-o " key" = value "\fR, \fP" \-\-option " key" = value
Override a top-level configuration key; may be repeated. Values are parsed as
Python literals where possible and are never executed.
.SS Experimental
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-experimental
Required by the experimental features below.
.TP
.B \-\-queue\-nodes
Show idle and total node counts per queue (requires
.BR \-e ).
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-web
Serve the view on
.I http://127.0.0.1:8080/
(requires
.BR \-e ).
Only
.IR / ,
.I /index.html
and
.I /api.json
are served. There is no login or TLS; change the address with
.B experimental_web_host
and
.B experimental_web_port
only behind an authenticating reverse proxy.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Print debug messages and operational-error tracebacks to standard error and
the log file.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity; may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
In watch mode
.RB ( \-w ):
.TP 16
.BR j " or " Space
down one screen
.TQ
.BR k " or " Backspace
up one screen
.TQ
.BR h " / " l
left / right one screen
.TQ
.BR g " or " K
top of the matrix
.TQ
.BR G " or " J
bottom of the matrix
.TQ
.BR 0 " / " $
left / right edge
.TQ
.B R
reset the viewport
.TQ
.B f
filter
.TQ
.B F
switch full names / numbered node labels
.TQ
.B H
highlight users or queues
.TQ
.B m
color cores by user / queue
.TQ
.B Q
expand / collapse the queue summary
.TQ
.B r
cycle all / real / used core lines
.TQ
.B s
sort
.TQ
.B t
transpose the matrix
.TQ
.B ?
toggle help
.TQ
.B q
quit
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read in this order, later ones replacing earlier ones:
.IP 1. 4
the bundled
.I qtopconf.yaml
.IP 2. 4
.I /etc/qtopconf.yaml
.IP 3. 4
.I $HOME/.local/qtop/qtopconf.yaml
.IP 4. 4
the file given with
.BR \-f ;
a relative name is looked up in
.I $HOME/.local/qtop
and then in the current directory
.IP 5. 4
each
.B \-o
override, from left to right
.PP
A file replaces whole top-level values; nested mappings such as
.B schedulers
are not merged. The scheduler is chosen by
.BR \-b ,
then
.BR QTOP_SCHEDULER ,
then the
.B scheduler
key.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QTOP_SCHEDULER
Scheduler to use when
.B \-b
is not given.
.TP
.B QTOP_COLOR
With
.BR "\-c AUTO" :
.B ON
forces color; any other value disables it; when unset, color is used on a
terminal.
.TP
.BR HOME ", " USER
Locate the per-user configuration and log, and expand the default
.IR savepath .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qtopconf.yaml
site configuration
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/qtop/qtopconf.yaml
user configuration
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/qtop/logs/qtop.log
log file (mode 0600)
.TP
.I /tmp/qtop_results_$USER
default
.IR savepath :
saved scheduler output and replay data, created with mode 0700
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
no usable scheduler, or an operational error (failed or timed-out scheduler
command, unreadable input, invalid configuration)
.TP
.B 2
invalid command-line arguments
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B qtop \-b demo
Show a synthetic cluster.
.TP
.B qtop \-w 10
Refresh every 10 seconds, auto-detecting the scheduler.
.TP
.B qtop \-b slurm \-c OFF \-1 \-3
Print only the occupancy matrix, without color.
.TP
.B qtop \-R 1823 1h
Replay one hour starting today at 18:23.
.TP
.B qtop \-e \-A \-L
Create a masked support archive.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR squeue (1),
.BR sinfo (1),
.BR qstat (1),
.BR pbsnodes (8),
.BR oarstat (1),
.BR watch (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
